+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Voyage 1: TodoMVC
+
+**Status:** Specs authored, watchbill written. Awaiting QM dispatch.
+
+**Specs authored:**
+- `features/add-and-display-todos.feature` — 7 scenarios
+- `features/toggle-todo.feature` — 7 scenarios
+- `features/edit-todo.feature` — 7 scenarios
+- `features/active-counter.feature` — 5 scenarios
+- `features/clear-completed.feature` — 5 scenarios
+- `features/filtering-routing.feature` — 7 scenarios
+- `features/persistence.feature` — 4 scenarios
+
+**Total:** 42 scenarios across 7 features.
+
+**Design decisions:**
+- Feature-per-concern split, not one monolithic feature. Each feature has one quality concern and one set of step definitions.
+- Editing is its own feature because it has distinct interaction rules (double-click, blur, Escape, trim-and-destroy-empty).
+- Routing and filtering combined: the spec treats them as inseparable — the filter state IS the route.
+- Persistence is a separate feature, not embedded in every other feature. It tests the reload seam independently.
+- No `@contract` scenarios: no scantling specified mechanical shape for this app.
+- No `@conformance` scenarios: no methodology checks on first voyage.
+
+**Assets referenced:**
+- `assets/app-spec.md` — TodoMVC spec (source of truth for behaviour)
+- `assets/app-template.index.html` — Base HTML markup
+
+**Next role:** QM, with clean context per the Context bulkhead Article.
diff --git a/features/active-counter.feature b/features/active-counter.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..18d4757
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/active-counter.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+Feature: Active todo counter
+  As a user
+  I want to see how many todos are left
+  So that I know my remaining workload
+
+  Rule: Counter shows active todo count
+
+    Scenario: Counter shows zero when no active todos
+      Given the todo list contains completed "Buy groceries"
+      Then the counter shows "0 items left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter shows singular for one active todo
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter shows plural for multiple active todos
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      And the todo list contains "Walk the dog"
+      Then the counter shows "2 items left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter updates when todo is completed
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      And the todo list contains "Walk the dog"
+      When the user toggles "Buy groceries"
+      Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter updates when completed todo is uncompleted
+      Given the todo list contains completed "Buy groceries"
+      And the todo list contains completed "Walk the dog"
+      When the user toggles "Buy groceries"
+      Then the counter shows "1 item left"
diff --git a/features/add-and-display-todos.feature b/features/add-and-display-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..abd76f6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/add-and-display-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+Feature: Add and display todos
+  As a user
+  I want to add new todos and see them in the list
+  So that I can track what needs to be done
+
+  Rule: New todos are added through the input field
+
+    Scenario: Adding a todo with Enter key
+      Given the todo list is empty
+      When the user types "Buy groceries" in the new todo input
+      And the user presses Enter
+      Then the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      And the new todo input is empty
+
+    Scenario: Empty or whitespace input is ignored
+      Given the todo list is empty
+      When the user types "   " in the new todo input
+      And the user presses Enter
+      Then the todo list is empty
+
+    Scenario: Input is trimmed before adding
+      Given the todo list is empty
+      When the user types "  Buy groceries  " in the new todo input
+      And the user presses Enter
+      Then the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+
+    Scenario: Multiple todos can be added
+      Given the todo list is empty
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+      And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+      Then the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      And the todo list contains "Walk the dog"
+
+  Rule: Todo visibility
+
+    Scenario: Newly added todos are active
+      Given the todo list is empty
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+      Then "Buy groceries" is not completed
+
+    Scenario: Empty state hides main section and footer
+      Given the todo list is empty
+      Then the main section is hidden
+      And the footer is hidden
+
+    Scenario: Non-empty state shows main section and footer
+      Given the todo list is empty
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy groceries"
+      Then the main section is visible
+      And the footer is visible
+
+  Rule: Input is focused on page load
+
+    Scenario: New todo input has focus when page loads
+      Then the new todo input is focused
diff --git a/features/clear-completed.feature b/features/clear-completed.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..32898ea
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/clear-completed.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+Feature: Clear completed todos
+  As a user
+  I want to remove all completed todos
+  So that I can clean up my list
+
+  Rule: Clear completed removes completed todos
+
+    Scenario: Clear completed removes completed todos
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      And the todo list contains completed "Walk the dog"
+      When the user clicks the clear completed button
+      Then the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      And the todo list does not contain "Walk the dog"
+
+    Scenario: Clear completed does not affect active todos
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      And the todo list contains "Walk the dog"
+      When the user clicks the clear completed button
+      Then the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      And the todo list contains "Walk the dog"
+
+  Rule: Clear completed button visibility
+
+    Scenario: Button is hidden when no completed todos exist
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      Then the clear completed button is hidden
+
+    Scenario: Button is visible when completed todos exist
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      And the todo list contains completed "Walk the dog"
+      Then the clear completed button is visible
+
+    Scenario: Button hides after all completed are cleared
+      Given the todo list contains completed "Buy groceries"
+      When the user clicks the clear completed button
+      Then the clear completed button is hidden
diff --git a/features/edit-todo.feature b/features/edit-todo.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5eeb4ac
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/edit-todo.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@
+Feature: Edit todo
+  As a user
+  I want to edit existing todos
+  So that I can correct or update my task descriptions
+
+  Rule: Double-click activates editing mode
+
+    Scenario: Double-clicking a todo shows the edit input
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      When the user double-clicks "Buy groceries"
+      Then "Buy groceries" is in editing mode
+      And the edit input contains "Buy groceries"
+
+    Scenario: Edit input is focused when editing mode activates
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      When the user double-clicks "Buy groceries"
+      Then the edit input is focused
+
+  Rule: Editing saves on blur and Enter
+
+    Scenario: Pressing Enter saves the edit
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      When the user double-clicks "Buy groceries"
+      And the user types "Buy organic groceries" in the edit input
+      And the user presses Enter in the edit input
+      Then the todo list contains "Buy organic groceries"
+      And "Buy organic groceries" is not in editing mode
+
+    Scenario: Blurring saves the edit
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      When the user double-clicks "Buy groceries"
+      And the user types "Buy organic groceries" in the edit input
+      And the user blurs the edit input
+      Then the todo list contains "Buy organic groceries"
+      And "Buy organic groceries" is not in editing mode
+
+  Rule: Empty edits destroy the todo
+
+    Scenario: Saving an empty edit removes the todo
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      When the user double-clicks "Buy groceries"
+      And the user clears the edit input
+      And the user presses Enter in the edit input
+      Then the todo list does not contain "Buy groceries"
+
+    Scenario: Saving a whitespace-only edit removes the todo
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      When the user double-clicks "Buy groceries"
+      And the user types "   " in the edit input
+      And the user presses Enter in the edit input
+      Then the todo list does not contain "Buy groceries"
+
+  Rule: Escape discards changes
+
+    Scenario: Pressing Escape discards the edit
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      When the user double-clicks "Buy groceries"
+      And the user types "Something else" in the edit input
+      And the user presses Escape in the edit input
+      Then the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      And "Buy groceries" is not in editing mode
+
+  Rule: Edit input is trimmed
+
+    Scenario: Edit input is trimmed before saving
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      When the user double-clicks "Buy groceries"
+      And the user types "  Buy organic groceries  " in the edit input
+      And the user presses Enter in the edit input
+      Then the todo list contains "Buy organic groceries"
diff --git a/features/filtering-routing.feature b/features/filtering-routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1299504
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/filtering-routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+Feature: Filtering and routing
+  As a user
+  I want to filter todos by status
+  So that I can focus on active or completed work
+
+  Rule: Default view shows all todos
+
+    Scenario: All todos are visible on the default route
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      And the todo list contains completed "Walk the dog"
+      When the user navigates to "#/"
+      Then "Buy groceries" is visible
+      And "Walk the dog" is visible
+      And "All" filter is selected
+
+  Rule: Active filter shows only active todos
+
+    Scenario: Active filter hides completed todos
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      And the todo list contains completed "Walk the dog"
+      When the user navigates to "#/active"
+      Then "Buy groceries" is visible
+      And "Walk the dog" is not visible
+      And "Active" filter is selected
+
+  Rule: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+
+    Scenario: Completed filter hides active todos
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      And the todo list contains completed "Walk the dog"
+      When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+      Then "Buy groceries" is not visible
+      And "Walk the dog" is visible
+      And "Completed" filter is selected
+
+  Rule: Items update when toggled in filtered view
+
+    Scenario: Completing a todo in Active filter hides it
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      And the todo list contains "Walk the dog"
+      When the user navigates to "#/active"
+      And the user toggles "Buy groceries"
+      Then "Buy groceries" is not visible
+      And "Walk the dog" is visible
+
+    Scenario: Uncompleting a todo in Completed filter hides it
+      Given the todo list contains completed "Buy groceries"
+      And the todo list contains completed "Walk the dog"
+      When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+      And the user toggles "Buy groceries"
+      Then "Buy groceries" is not visible
+      And "Walk the dog" is visible
+
+  Rule: Routing persists on reload
+
+    Scenario: Active filter persists after page reload
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      And the todo list contains completed "Walk the dog"
+      When the user navigates to "#/active"
+      And the page is reloaded
+      Then "Buy groceries" is visible
+      And "Walk the dog" is not visible
+      And "Active" filter is selected
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..aaf5bfc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+Feature: Persistence to localStorage
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to survive page reloads
+  So that I do not lose my data
+
+  Rule: Todos are saved to localStorage
+
+    Scenario: Todos persist after page reload
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      And the todo list contains "Walk the dog"
+      When the page is reloaded
+      Then the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      And the todo list contains "Walk the dog"
+
+    Scenario: Completed state persists after page reload
+      Given the todo list contains completed "Buy groceries"
+      When the page is reloaded
+      Then "Buy groceries" is completed
+
+    Scenario: Active state persists after page reload
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      When the page is reloaded
+      Then "Buy groceries" is not completed
+
+    Scenario: Deletions persist after page reload
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      And the todo list contains completed "Walk the dog"
+      When the user clicks the clear completed button
+      And the page is reloaded
+      Then the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      And the todo list does not contain "Walk the dog"
diff --git a/features/toggle-todo.feature b/features/toggle-todo.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..fa348eb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/toggle-todo.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+Feature: Toggle todo completion
+  As a user
+  I want to mark todos as complete or active
+  So that I can track my progress
+
+  Rule: Individual todos can be toggled
+
+    Scenario: Clicking the checkbox completes a todo
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      When the user toggles "Buy groceries"
+      Then "Buy groceries" is completed
+
+    Scenario: Clicking the checkbox again makes a todo active
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      When the user toggles "Buy groceries"
+      And the user toggles "Buy groceries"
+      Then "Buy groceries" is not completed
+
+  Rule: Mark all as complete checkbox
+
+    Scenario: Mark all as complete checks all todos
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      And the todo list contains "Walk the dog"
+      When the user clicks the toggle all checkbox
+      Then "Buy groceries" is completed
+      And "Walk the dog" is completed
+      And the toggle all checkbox is checked
+
+    Scenario: Unchecking mark all unchecks all todos
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      And the todo list contains "Walk the dog"
+      When the user clicks the toggle all checkbox
+      And the user clicks the toggle all checkbox
+      Then "Buy groceries" is not completed
+      And "Walk the dog" is not completed
+      And the toggle all checkbox is not checked
+
+    Scenario: Toggle all reflects individual states
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      And the todo list contains "Walk the dog"
+      When the user toggles "Buy groceries"
+      Then the toggle all checkbox is not checked
+      When the user toggles "Walk the dog"
+      Then the toggle all checkbox is checked
+
+    Scenario: Clearing all completed unchecks toggle all
+      Given the todo list contains "Buy groceries"
+      And the todo list contains "Walk the dog"
+      When the user toggles "Buy groceries"
+      And the user toggles "Walk the dog"
+      And the user clicks the clear completed button
+      Then the toggle all checkbox is not checked
